# Line endings are normalized to LF, in the repository AND in the working tree
# on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists: the regression gate (test/regression.sh) byte-compares
# freshly generated program output against the reference outputs committed under
# sample-output/, and CI runs that comparison on Linux, macOS and Windows. A
# Windows clone with the default core.autocrlf=true checks those references out
# with CRLF endings while the program writes LF, so the comparison fails on one
# platform out of three for a reason that has nothing to do with the physics.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than just `text=auto` is deliberate: it pins the working tree,
# not only the stored blob, so a byte compare means the same thing everywhere.
# Any modern editor handles LF on Windows.
#
# This file is the first half of the fix. The second half is that
# test/regression.sh normalizes line endings itself before comparing, instead of
# trusting checkout behaviour. Either alone would be enough on a good day; the
# gate is the foundation every later change is measured against, so it gets both.

*           text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out for the files the gate depends on, so the intent survives an edit
# to the wildcard above.
*.f         text eol=lf
*.out       text eol=lf
*.mfj       text eol=lf
*.in        text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf

# Never transform these. text=auto guesses from content and guesses well, but a
# reference PDF or an archive is not worth leaving to a heuristic.
*.pdf       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.gz        binary
*.zip       binary
